AWS reserves 5 IP addresses in every subnet — not just the usual "network" 
wand "broadcast" address like in normal networking.
So a /24 subnet (256 addresses) really only gives you 251 usable addresses. 
This trips people up a lot on the SAA exam.

Memory trick: think "first 4, last 1" — the first 4 addresses in the block are reserved 
(This website will help you calculate the CIDR "https://www.ipaddressguide.com/cidr")
(network, router, DNS, future-use) and the very last one is reserved (broadcast).

/32 	1	One single house
/24	 256	A small neighborhood
/16	 65,536	A small city
/8	16 million+	A whole country
