                                    VPC Endpoint
AWS VPC Endpoint is a general term for a way to connect resources in your VPC to AWS services privately, without needing the public internet.

                                                Types of Endpoint
interface Endpoint:
provision an ENI (private Ip addresses) as an entry point (must attach security groups)
An AWS Interface Endpoint is a way for resources inside your VPC to access an AWS service privately, 
without going through the public internet, NAT Gateway, or an Internet Gateway.

Gateway Endpoint:
provision a Gateway and must be  used as a target in a route table (does not use security groups)
supports both S3 and DynamoDB and it's free
 
ipv4 Troubleshooting 
ipv4 cannot be disabled for your vpc and subnet
so if you cannot launch an ec2 instances in your subnet
it not Because it cannot acquire an ipv6 
it Because there are no available ipv4 in your subnet

solution: create a new ipv4 CIDR in your subnet
 


